From 6f6eedad81b22b5e93bfb69b1c611800b38dfb1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 20:41:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] Bump xdg_wm_base 1 to 6

Replace the vendored xdg-shell.xml (previously xdg_toplevel v3, no
configure_bounds/wm_capabilities/suspended) with current upstream, and
advertise version 6.

xdg_wm_base.create_positioner and xdg_surface.get_popup were both
complete no-op stubs (a positioner that discarded every request, a
popup that sent popup_done immediately). Since older clients could
only bind version 1, xdg_popup_interface.reposition (added in v3) was
never wired up; advertising v6 would let a real client call it against
a NULL handler and crash the compositor. Replace both stubs: a real
OwlXdgPositioner records size/anchor-rect/anchor/gravity/offset and
computes popup geometry from them (constraint_adjustment is accepted
but not applied - the popup is placed unconstrained, which is
spec-compliant for the "none" adjustment and a reasonable
approximation otherwise), and OwlXdgPopup sends real configure events
and implements reposition as recompute + repositioned + configure +
xdg_surface.configure, per spec order. grab is accepted as a no-op
rather than left unimplemented, since owl has no separate popup input
grab machinery.

xdg_toplevel gains the v4-v6 additions: configure_bounds (visible
screen frame) before every configure, a wm_capabilities event sent
once at creation (maximize/fullscreen/minimize; no window_menu), and
suspended state tracked via windowDidMiniaturize:/windowDidDeminiaturize:
and appended to makeStates when the bound version supports it.

Also fixes get_xdg_surface, get_toplevel, and get_popup to pass the
parent resource's bound version through to wl_resource_create instead
of hardcoding 1, matching the decoration-manager bind pattern.
